ow there are  majorities in this country who  say that they will go and vote in the  favor of the climate that is i think  that is  pretty big but again that is one part of  the puzzle piece  and yet what we still need is this kind  of action  the kind of effective emission reduction  and obviously people everywhere  starting to you know become part of the  solution well yes and you say  talk about the election as you say it's  a few months away but the green party  is doing well in the polls isn't it do  you think that a chancellor from de  gruner is realistic  um well we never had any kind of  election like this where actually you  know  there were the greens you know putting  forward a chance la canada  um by the end of the day this isn't up  to a particular chancellor no matter  from which party but this is about  a broad consensus that we need on 1.5  degree politics and this needs to be you  know  um bipartisan we need parties in the  entire democratic spectrum in germany to  understand that this isn't question  if we do climate actions or what kind of  climate action we do  that is where we need to have the debate  and this one election won't solve the  you know the climate action that is  needed in germany  ideally we end up with a election result  that can  again provide a foundation for further  work that needs to be done  and that is not a single person that  will change it but it's  rather the general the the vibe the um  attention on the issue and how far would  you take your environmental fight would  you take it into politics would you run  for office  well i i kind of i think i decided i  want to do everything i can  to to fight for climate justice wherever  this is most effective and  what we see right now is that activism  any kind of activism can change  everything and so as an activist i see  that  you know this is needed much more maybe  at some point we get to a stage where i  feel okay  my work as an activist on the street and  the movement  isn't as needed anymore maybe as it  could be somewhere else and then  we need to chat again but you know if  you would have asked me five years ago  what would you do in five years i would  have never imagined to to to do what i  do right now  so i've grown very conscious about  making any assumptions about my future  keeping your options open  well yes that as well okay louisa nobel  really good to talk to you thanks very  much indeed thank you
 

